{
  "info": {
    "name": "Bitcoin Tracker API",
    "description": "# Bitcoin Tracker API\n\nCompares the current Bitcoin price with the target prices you set. When the price drops below a target (like in a flash crash), the API sends an SMS through Twilio.\n\n**Legal disclaimer:** Cryptocurrencies are volatile. This API assumes no ownership or liability for any gain or loss. Use responsibly.\n\n## Quickstart\n\n1. Run the Laravel server (`php artisan serve`) with the variables from `.env.example` filled in on the server.\n2. Import `Bitcoin Tracker.postman_environment.json` and select the **Bitcoin Tracker** environment.\n3. Set `baseUrl` and `apiKey` (must match `TRACKER_API_KEY` on the server).\n4. Run **Create Alert**, then **Check Alerts**.\n\n## Environment variables (Postman)\n\n| Variable | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `baseUrl` | Base URL of the API, e.g. `http://localhost:8000` |\n| `apiKey` | Value sent in the `X-API-Key` header |\n| `alertId` | Filled automatically by **Create Alert**; used by **Delete Alert** |\n\n## Server configuration (not stored in Postman)\n\nTwilio credentials stay on the server in `.env`: `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, `TWILIO_FROM`. They are never part of this collection or its environment.\n\n## Authentication\n\nEvery request needs the `X-API-Key` header. Requests are limited to 60 per minute.\n\n## Cost warning\n\n`Check Alerts` sends real SMS messages and may incur Twilio charges.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "apikey",
    "apikey": [
      {
        "key": "key",
        "value": "X-API-Key",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "value",
        "value": "{{apiKey}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "in",
        "value": "header",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Get Bitcoin Rate",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/rate",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "rate"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Returns the current Bitcoin price in USD, fetched live from the price provider (CoinGecko by default)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Has a numeric rate', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.rate).to.be.a('number'));"
            ]
          }
        }
